  <content>
    <procedure>
      <mainProcedure>
        <proceduralStep>
          <para>Ensure the engine has been shut down for at least 30 minutes to allow oil to drain back to the sump.</para>
        </proceduralStep>
        <proceduralStep>
          <para>Position a suitable container under the oil drain valve.</para>
        </proceduralStep>
        <proceduralStep>
          <para>Open the oil drain valve and allow oil to drain completely.</para>
        </proceduralStep>
        <proceduralStep>
          <para>Close the oil drain valve and ensure it is properly secured.</para>
        </proceduralStep>
        <proceduralStep>
          <para>Remove and replace the oil filter element.</para>
        </proceduralStep>
        <proceduralStep>
          <para>Add the specified quantity of approved engine oil through the oil filler port.</para>
        </proceduralStep>
        <proceduralStep>
          <para>Check oil level using the dipstick and add oil as necessary to bring to the correct level.</para>
        </proceduralStep>
        <proceduralStep>
          <para>Run the engine for 5 minutes and recheck the oil level.</para>
        </proceduralStep>
      </mainProcedure>
    </procedure>
  </content>
